      "n": 1,
      "signpost": null,
      "definition": "one of two equal parts of a group or an amount",
      "explanation": "**Half** takes a plural verb when it refers to people or things that can be counted (*half of them are here*) and a singular verb for an amount (*half of it is gone*). Before **the**, **my**, **this**, and so on, **of** can be left out (*half the students*); that use is the determiner.",
      "grammar": {
        "countability": null,
        "transitivity": null,
